### Examples

**Minimal doc-commented library with build step.**

`src/math.zig`:
```zig
//! Mathematical constants and basic vector operations.

/// The circle constant.
pub const TAU = 6.283185307179586;

/// A 2D vector with floating-point components.
pub const Vec2 = struct {
    /// Horizontal component.
    x: f64,
    /// Vertical component.
    y: f64,

    /// Computes the squared Euclidean length.
    pub fn lengthSquared(self: Vec2) f64 {
        return self.x * self.x + self.y * self.y;
    }
};
```

`build.zig`:
```zig
const std = @import("std");

pub fn build(b: *std.Build) void {
    const target = b.standardTargetOptions(.{});
    const optimize = b.standardOptimizeOption(.{});

    const lib = b.addStaticLibrary(.{
        .name = "math",
        .root_source_file = b.path("src/math.zig"),
        .target = target,
        .optimize = optimize,
    });

    const docs = b.step("docs", "Generate documentation");
    docs.dependOn(&lib.emit_docs.step);
}
```

Running `zig build docs` creates `zig-out/docs/index.html`, `data.json`, and `search_index.json`. Open `index.html` to see a navigable (if plain) representation.

**Extracting the JSON for custom processing.** The `data.json` can be parsed with any JSON library. A simple Zig program that prints all function signatures:

```zig
const std = @import("std");
const json = std.json;

pub fn main() !void {
    var gpa = std.heap.GeneralPurposeAllocator(.{}){};
    defer _ = gpa.deinit();
    const allocator = gpa.allocator();

    const args = try std.process.argsAlloc(allocator);
    defer std.process.argsFree(allocator, args);
    if (args.len < 2) return error.Usage;

    const file = try std.fs.cwd().openFile(args[1], .{});
    defer file.close();
    const contents = try file.readToEndAlloc(allocator, 10 * 1024 * 1024);
    defer allocator.free(contents);

    var tree = try json.parseFromSlice(json.Value, allocator, contents, .{});
    defer tree.deinit();

    // Walk the root module looking for public functions.
    const root = tree.value.object.get("decls") orelse return;
    for (root.array.items) |decl| {
        if (decl.object.get("kind")) |kind| {
            if (std.mem.eql(u8, kind.string, "function")) {
                std.debug.print("{s}\n", .{decl.object.get("name").?.string});
            }
        }
    }
}
```

